  "source_path": "/scratch/ziv_baretto/Thesis_Ziv/Capstone-Thesis-/DATA_SET_BUILDER_AND_EXPLORER/Timeline_Maker/output_merged_v3/food_safety/Shri.Hanamant Appasab Shirahatti vs The State Of Karnataka on 7 July, 2020.json",
  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shri.Hanamant Appasab Shirahatti vs The State Of Karnataka on",
    "facts": "ORDER This petition is filed by accused under section 438 of Cr.P.C., for release on bail in the event of his arrest in Crime No.28/2020 of Aigali P.S., Dist: Belagavi, registered for the offences punishable under sections 272, 273, 328 of IPC and under sections 54, 57, 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act 2006 and Food Safety and Standard Rules, 2011. 2. The facts briefly stated in the petition are that, on the report submitted by the Police Inspector DCIB unit, Belagavi, the police have registered the case. The allegations are that, on receiving credible information about the adulteration of milk, the complainant Police Inspector and other staff visited Junjarwad village and conducted raid in a shed at the place R.S.No.143 where a person called UmarAli Hajisab Ansari was involved in adulterating the milk with some materials which are hazardous to the life of the people. The material found in the spot were seized. On enquiry, accused No.1 UmarAli Hajaresab Ansari informed that the petitioner Hanamant Appasab Shirahatti is providing the materials for adulteration. Thus, on the said information the police have registered the case against the petitioner and he has been arraigned as accused No.2. On registering the complaint, the police officials are making attempts to arrest the petitioner.",
    "arguments": "4. It is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that only on the basis of the information said to have been disclosed by accused No.1, who has been apprehended at the spot, the police officers have falsely implicated the petitioner in this case. There is no convincing material evidence to show that the petitioner was supplying the material for adulteration. In the event of arrest and detention, the petitioner would be put to great hardship. 5. Per contra, the learned HCGP submitted that as per the information it is evident that the petitioner was supplying the hazardous material for adulteration of milk which affects the health of the consumers. Thus, having committed the heinous crime, the petitioner is not entitled for bail. The complaint averments disclose that on the basis of the information given by accused No.1, the petitioner has been arraigned as accused No.2.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. It is the submission of the learned counsel for the petitioner that only on the basis of the information said to have been disclosed by accused No.1, who has been apprehended at the spot, the police officers have falsely implicated the petitioner in this case. There is no convincing material evidence to show that the petitioner was supplying the material for adulteration. In the event of arrest and detention, the petitioner would be put to great hardship. 5. Per contra, the learned HCGP submitted that as per the information it is evident that the petitioner was supplying the hazardous material for adulteration of milk which affects the health of the consumers. Thus, having committed the heinous crime, the petitioner is not entitled for bail.",
    "respondent_arguments": "The complaint averments disclose that on the basis of the information given by accused No.1, the petitioner has been arraigned as accused No.2.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
